  "description": "Research and Related Senior/Key Person Profile (Expanded) (RR_KeyPersonExpanded_4_0) is the expanded version of the R&R Senior/Key Person Profile form. It adds Degree Type and Degree Year fields to the person profile and is the most widely used form in this category, appearing in 7.89% of all grant applications.",
  "sgg_form_id": "rr_key_person_expanded",
  "notes": [
    "State/ZIP requirement: DAT shows asterisks on State and ZIP for Key Person entries, implying they are always required. The XSD marks both as optional. Resolution: follow the XSD. State is conditionally required when Country is USA.",
    "BioSketch requirement for Key Person: DAT implies BioSketch is required for Key Person. The XSD marks BioSketchsAttached as minOccurs=\"0\" within the KeyPerson profile. Resolution: follow the XSD. BioSketch is optional for Key Person but required for PD/PI.",
    "Department/Division maxLength: The XSD uses V2 types with maxLength 100. We use the XSD constraint (100).",
    "ZIP/Postal Code maxLength: XSD defines maxLength 30. We use the XSD constraint (30).",
    "DegreeType maxLength: XSD allows up to 75 characters. We use the XSD constraint (75).",
    "DegreeYear maxLength: XSD allows up to 25 characters (not just 4). We use the XSD constraint (25) but may add UI guidance for a 4-digit year format."
  ],
  "risks": [
    "This is the highest-volume Key Personnel form (321K submissions, 7.89% of applications) and should be prioritized",
    "Very similar to the base R&R Senior/Key Person Profile (FID 772), only adds Degree Type and Degree Year. A shared component approach is strongly recommended.",
    "BioSketch attachment requirement differs between PD/PI (required) and Key Person (optional), unlike the base form where it is required for both",
    "The Key Person section allows up to 99 entries (XSD maxOccurs=99)",
    "State and ZIP/Postal Code show asterisks in the DAT for Key Person (implying required) but the XSD marks them optional. The XSD is authoritative for required/optional."
  ],
